stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR
    state "active" as active
    state "expiring_soon" as expiring_soon
    state "frozen" as frozen
    state "expired" as expired

    [*] --> active: purchase or confirmed VNPay [eligible] / create active membership
    active --> expiring_soon: hourly sync [0..7 days remain] / persist expiring_soon
    active --> expired: hourly sync [expiry passed] / persist expired
    expiring_soon --> active: renewal [coverage extended beyond 7 days] / extend expiry
    expiring_soon --> expired: hourly sync [expiry passed] / persist expired
    active --> frozen: freeze effective [approved range contains today] / persist frozen
    expiring_soon --> frozen: freeze effective [approved range contains today] / persist frozen
    frozen --> active: hourly sync [freeze ended and >7 days remain] / persist active
    frozen --> expiring_soon: hourly sync [freeze ended and <=7 days remain] / persist expiring_soon
    frozen --> expired: hourly sync [expiry passed] / persist expired
    expired --> active: FSM rule only [expired row] / no runtime renewal writer

    note bottom of frozen
        Derivation order is active freeze window, expired date,
        0..7 days remaining, then active.
    end note
    note bottom of expired
        Expired self-service purchase creates a new active row.
        It does not mutate the old expired row back to active.
    end note
